"use strict";(self.webpackChunksmart_barcode_scan_and_ordering_doc=self.webpackChunksmart_barcode_scan_and_ordering_doc||[]).push([[133],{2674(e,t,a){a.r(t),a.d(t,{_pageData:()=>o,default:()=>n});var r=a(641);const o=JSON.parse('{"path":"/smart-barcode-scan/taxes-and-order-totals.html","title":"Taxes & Order Totals","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"title":"Taxes & Order Totals","description":"How the Smart Barcode Scan console calculates the running total of a counter order, how tax and shipping tax are handled, and how the figures on a scanned order are read."},"git":{},"filePathRelative":"smart-barcode-scan/taxes-and-order-totals.md"}'),s={name:"taxes-and-order-totals.md"},n=(0,a(6262).A)(s,[["render",function(e,t,a,o,s,n){const i=(0,r.g2)("RouteLink");return(0,r.uX)(),(0,r.CE)("div",null,[t[4]||(t[4]=(0,r.Fv)('<h1 id="taxes-order-totals" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#taxes-order-totals"><span>Taxes &amp; Order Totals</span></a></h1><p>Two different totals appear in the console, and it is worth knowing which is which:</p><ul><li>The <strong>running total in Create Order</strong> is a live preview, worked out in the browser while you build the cart.</li><li>The <strong>totals on a scanned order</strong> are the figures WooCommerce itself stored when the order was created.</li></ul><h2 id="the-running-total-in-create-order" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#the-running-total-in-create-order"><span>The running total in Create Order</span></a></h2><p>The <strong>ORDER TOTAL</strong> block sits at the bottom of the item list. Click <strong>View Details</strong> to expand the breakdown.</p><p><img src="/smart-barcode-scan-and-ordering/images/smart-barcode-scan/smart-barcode-create-order-totals.png" alt="The order totals breakdown in Create Order"></p><table><thead><tr><th>Line</th><th>Shown when</th><th>How it is worked out</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Items Subtotal</strong></td><td>Always</td><td>For each item: its sale price if one is set, otherwise its regular price, multiplied by the quantity</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Coupon Discount</strong></td><td>A coupon is applied and the discount is above zero</td><td>Estimated from the coupon&#39;s type and restrictions — see below</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Shipping (<code>method</code>)</strong></td><td>A shipping method is selected, or the cost is above zero</td><td>The cost of the selected method</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Tax (incl.) / Tax (excl.)</strong></td><td>WooCommerce taxes are enabled and the tax is above zero</td><td>Product tax plus shipping tax — see below</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Order Total</strong></td><td>Always</td><td>The final figure, matching the collapsed <strong>ORDER TOTAL</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="how-tax-is-estimated" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#how-tax-is-estimated"><span>How tax is estimated</span></a></h2><p>Tax appears only when <strong>taxes are enabled in WooCommerce</strong> (<strong>WooCommerce → Settings → General → Enable taxes</strong>). With taxes turned off, no tax line is shown and no tax is added.</p><p>When taxes are on:</p><ul><li>Each item uses the rate for <strong>its own tax class</strong>, falling back to the standard rate if that class has no rate defined.</li><li>Items whose tax status is <em>None</em> are skipped.</li><li>With <strong>prices entered exclusive of tax</strong>, the tax is added on top of the line total, and the label reads <strong>Tax (excl.)</strong>.</li><li>With <strong>prices entered inclusive of tax</strong>, the tax already contained in the price is shown separately and is <em>not</em> added again, and the label reads <strong>Tax (incl.)</strong>.</li></ul><div class="hint-container important"><p class="hint-container-title">Important</p><p>The rates used for this preview come from your <strong>store&#39;s base location</strong> — the country and state set in <strong>WooCommerce → Settings → General</strong>. They are not recalculated for the customer&#39;s address. If your store charges tax based on the customer&#39;s address, the preview is an estimate; the definitive tax is calculated by WooCommerce when the order is created.</p></div><h2 id="how-shipping-tax-is-handled" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#how-shipping-tax-is-handled"><span>How shipping tax is handled</span></a></h2><p>When you click <strong>Calculate Shipping</strong>, each returned method carries its own cost and its own tax status:</p><ul><li>A <strong>taxable</strong> method contributes shipping tax. If WooCommerce returned a tax amount for the rate, that amount is used; otherwise the standard base rate is applied to the shipping cost.</li><li>A method whose tax status is <strong>None</strong> contributes no tax.</li><li>Shipping tax is added into the single <strong>Tax</strong> line rather than being shown separately.</li></ul><p>With tax-inclusive pricing, the method dropdown shows the tax-inclusive cost so the figure matches what the customer pays.</p><h2 id="how-coupon-discounts-are-estimated" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#how-coupon-discounts-are-estimated"><span>How coupon discounts are estimated</span></a></h2><p>Applying a coupon validates it against your store first, then the console estimates the discount by working through the cart:</p><ul><li>Items excluded by product ID or by product category are skipped.</li><li>If the coupon is limited to specific products or categories, only those items count.</li><li>If the coupon excludes sale items, items currently on sale are skipped.</li><li><strong>Percentage</strong> coupons take that percentage of every eligible line.</li><li><strong>Fixed product</strong> coupons take the fixed amount off each eligible unit, never more than the unit price.</li><li><strong>Fixed cart</strong> coupons take the fixed amount off the eligible subtotal, never more than that subtotal.</li></ul><p>The total discount is capped at the items subtotal, so a cart can never fall below zero.</p><div class="hint-container note"><p class="hint-container-title">Note</p><p>This is a preview. The amounts recorded on the finished order are recalculated by WooCommerce, which applies its own coupon rules — including minimum and maximum spend, per-user limits and individual-use restrictions.</p></div><h2 id="what-happens-when-the-order-is-created" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#what-happens-when-the-order-is-created"><span>What happens when the order is created</span></a></h2><p>Clicking <strong>CREATE</strong> hands the cart to WooCommerce, which:</p><ol><li>Adds each product at the quantity you set.</li><li>Adds the selected shipping method as a shipping line.</li><li>Calculates the totals, including tax, using your live WooCommerce tax settings.</li><li>Applies each coupon you added and recalculates the totals again.</li><li>Saves the order in the status you chose.</li></ol><p>Because step 3 and step 4 are WooCommerce&#39;s own calculations, <strong>the saved order is authoritative</strong>. Always confirm the total on the created order rather than relying on the preview when the two could differ — for example when tax is charged by customer address.</p><p><img src="/smart-barcode-scan-and-ordering/images/smart-barcode-scan/smart-barcode-created-order-woocommerce.png" alt="The created order in WooCommerce"></p><h2 id="totals-on-a-scanned-order" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#totals-on-a-scanned-order"><span>Totals on a scanned order</span></a></h2><p>Scan an existing order and click <strong>View Details</strong> on its <strong>ORDER TOTAL</strong> block.</p><p><img src="/smart-barcode-scan-and-ordering/images/smart-barcode-scan/smart-barcode-order-totals.png" alt="The totals breakdown on a scanned order"></p><p>This breakdown reads straight from the order:</p><table><thead><tr><th>Line</th><th>Source</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Items Subtotal</strong></td><td>The order&#39;s item subtotal</td></tr><tr><td>Each tax line, by its own label</td><td>The tax lines recorded on the order, each combining its item tax and shipping tax</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Shipping</strong></td><td>The order&#39;s shipping total</td></tr><tr><td>Each coupon, by its code</td><td>The coupon lines recorded on the order, shown as a negative amount</td></tr><tr><td>Any fee, by its name</td><td>The fee lines recorded on the order</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Grand Total</strong></td><td>The order total</td></tr></tbody></table><p>When an order has no tax lines, a single <strong>Tax</strong> row is shown with the order&#39;s total tax — normally zero. When it has no coupons, a single <strong>Coupon Discount</strong> row is shown with the order&#39;s discount total.</p><p>All amounts are formatted in the order&#39;s own currency, which may differ from your current store currency for older orders.</p><h2 id="next-step" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#next-step"><span>Next step</span></a></h2>',34)),(0,r.Lk)("ul",null,[(0,r.Lk)("li",null,[(0,r.bF)(i,{to:"/smart-barcode-scan/create-order.html"},{default:(0,r.k6)(()=>[...t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,r.eW)("Create Order",-1)])]),_:1}),t[1]||(t[1]=(0,r.eW)(" — the full order-building flow.",-1))]),(0,r.Lk)("li",null,[(0,r.bF)(i,{to:"/smart-barcode-scan/order-scanning.html"},{default:(0,r.k6)(()=>[...t[2]||(t[2]=[(0,r.eW)("Order Scanning",-1)])]),_:1}),t[3]||(t[3]=(0,r.eW)(" — the rest of the order screen.",-1))])])])}]])}}]);